Plugin H: SCM Webhook Ingestion & GitLab Code Extraction
============================================================

Purpose:
Ingest SCM webhook events, retrieve related code changes via SCM APIs,
and persist aggregated code as reviewable input for downstream workflows.

Activation:

- method name or purpose includes:
  webhook | gitlab | scm | repository event | code ingestion

- method description mentions:
  webhook payload | commit | diff | source code | CI integration

- entity_operations include create of:
  ReviewEvent | CodeEvent | SourceSnapshot

============================================================
Mandatory Capabilities
============================================================

H-1. Webhook Validation
- Validate required fields:
  - source identifier
  - repository / project identifier
  - commit list
- Missing fields → ValueError("InvalidInput")
- Empty commits → ValueError or domain error

H-2. SCM API Diff Retrieval
- Fetch code diffs using identifiers from webhook payload
- API calls MUST be real and executed
- Authentication MUST come from runtime config (env / app config)
- Hard-coded tokens or endpoints are FORBIDDEN

Canonical SCM Example (GitLab):

When source == "gitlab":

- Payload provides:
  - project_id
  - commits[].id (commit SHA)
- Diffs MUST be fetched via:
  GET /projects/{project_id}/repository/commits/{commit_sha}/diff
- Authentication via:
  PRIVATE-TOKEN header
- Diff response MUST be parsed and extracted

Other SCM providers MAY be supported, but GitLab is the canonical reference.

H-3. Deterministic Code Assembly
- Aggregate all fetched diffs into a single textual representation
- Ordering MUST be stable (commit order as received)
- Include commit and file boundaries
- Output MUST be suitable for analysis (LLM or rules)

H-4. Persistence
- Persist aggregated code as a new entity (e.g., ReviewEvent)
- Use repository.create(...) ONLY
- Service manages transaction boundary:
  - commit once on success
  - rollback once on failure

H-5. Traceable Output
- Return identifiers of persisted entity (e.g., event_id, state)
- Returning raw webhook payload is NOT allowed

============================================================
Explicit Prohibitions
============================================================

- Hard-coded SCM tokens or API URLs
- Skipping diff retrieval while claiming success
- Persisting empty or partial code
- Performing analysis or AI inference in this plugin

============================================================
Failure Handling
============================================================

- SCM API failure → RuntimeError
- No commits / no diffs → ValueError or domain-specific error
- Persistence failure → rollback and re-raise




